  "content": {
    "id": "p7-p3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Simplify\n$$\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac12\\right)+\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac23\\right)+\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac34\\right)+\\cdots+\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{99}{100}\\right).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-2$\n\nCombine the logarithms. The factors from $2$ to $99$ cancel in the product.",
      "worked": "Let $S$ be the given sum. By the product law,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac12\\times\\frac23\\times\\frac34\\times\\cdots\\times\\frac{99}{100}\\right)\\\\S&=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac1{100}\\right)\\\\S&=\\log_{10}(10^{-2})\\\\S&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nIn the product each integer from $2$ to $99$ occurs once in a numerator and once in a denominator.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 26
  },
